{"strongs": "H2454", "word": "חָכְמה", "translit": "chokh.mot", "root": "חכל", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "wisdom", "definition": "חָכְמה noun feminine wisdom , ׳ ח Exod 28:3 + 106 t.; construct חָכְמַת Exod 35:35 + 15 t.; suffix חָכְמָתִי Eccl 2:9 , etc. + 25 t. suffix; plural abstract emphatic חָכְמוֺת Ps 49:4 ; Prov 1:20 ; Prov 9:1 ; Prov 24:7 חַכְמוֺת Prov 14:1 (in correctly pointed as adjective construct f.; read חָכְמוֺת De ); — 1. skill in war Isa 10:13 in technical work Exod 28:3 ; Exod 31:3 ; Exod 31:6 ; Exod 35:26 ; Exod 35:31 ; Exod 35:35 ; Exod 36:1 ; Exod 36:2 ( P ), compare 1Kgs 7:14 ; 1Chr 28:21 of sailors Ps 107:27 . 2. wisdom , in administration Deut 34:9 ; Isa 29:14 ; Jer 49:7 (twice in verse); 2Sam 14:20 of prince of Tyre Ezek 28:4 ; Ezek 28:5 ; Ezek 28:7 ; Ezek 28:12 ; Ezek 29:12 ; Ezek 29:17 Solomon's wisdom included this with other forms of cleverness and shrewdness 1Kgs 2:6 ; 1Kgs 3:28 ; 1Kgs 5:9 ; 1Kgs 5:10 ; 1Kgs 5:14 (twice in verse); 1Kgs 5:26 ; 1Kgs 10:4 ; 1Kgs 10:6 ; 1Kgs 10:7 ; 1Kgs 10:8 ; 1Kgs 10:23 ; 1Kgs 10:24 = 2Chr 9:3 ; 2Chr 9:5 ; 2Chr 9:6 ; 2Chr 9:7 ; 2Chr 9:22 ; 2Chr 1:10 ; 2Chr 1:11 ; 2Chr 1:12 the Messiah is to have רוּחַ חָכְמָה וּבִינָה Isa 11:2 . 3. shrewdness, wisdom , 2Sam 20:22 ; 1Kgs 5:10 (twice in verse); Jer 9:22 withheld by God from the ostrich Job 39:17 of magicians and prophets Isa 47:10 ; Dan 1:4 ; Dan 1:17 ; Dan 1:20 . 4. wisdom, prudence in religious affairs Deut 4:6 ; Ps 37:30 ; Ps 51:8 ; Ps 90:12 ; Prov 10:31 ; Isa 33:6 ; Jer 8:9 5. wisdom , ethical and religious: \\ \\ a. of God, as a divine attribute or energy; his wisdom is in the skies Job 38:36 by it he numbers the clouds Job 38:37 founded the earth Prov 3:19 and made all things Jer 10:12 = Jer 51:15 , Ps 104:24 it is with him Job 12:13 not to be found by the most persevering human search Job 28:12 ; Job 28:20 he alone knows it Job 28:23 gives it Prov 2:6 and shows its secrets Job 11:6 . \\ \\ b. the divine wisdom is personified: she was begotten before all things to be the architect and counsellor of God in the creation ( Prov 8:22-31 ); she builds a palace and spreads a feast for those who will receive her instruction Prov 9:1 (compare v Prov 9:2-5 ); she teaches in public Prov 1:20 ; Prov 8:1 ; Prov 8:5 ; Prov 8:11 ; Prov 8:12 (see context); gives her pupils the divine spirit Prov 1:23 by her discipline simple become wise, rulers rule wisely, and those seeking her are richly rewarded Prov 8:14 (compare v Prov 8:1-21 ). \\ \\ c. of man: to get wisdom is principal thing Prov 4:7 (twice in verse); its fundamental principle is to fear God Ps 111:10 ; Prov 15:33 ; Job 28:18 (|| סוּר מֵרַע בִּינָה ); and know ׳ י , the All Holy Prov 9:10 ; Prov 30:3 it is of inestimable worth Job 28:18 ; Prov 8:11 ; Prov 16:16 ; Prov 17:16 ; Prov 23:23 ; Prov 24:7 beyond the reach of scorners Prov 14:6 God giveth it to the good Eccl 2:26 men are to incline the ear Prov 2:2 attend unto wisdom Prov 5:1 seek Eccl 7:25 know Prov 24:14 ; Eccl 1:17 ; Eccl 8:16 behold Eccl 2:12 ; Eccl 9:13 get her Prov 4:5 ; Prov 4:7 treat her as sister Prov 7:4 happy the man who finds her Prov 3:13 he who has wisdom is אִישׁ תְּבוּנָה Prov 10:23 נָבוֺן Prov 10:13 ; Prov 14:33 מֵבִין Prov 17:24 compare also Ps 49:4 ; Job 4:21 ; Job 12:2 ; Job 12:12 ; Job 13:5 ; Job 15:8 ; Job 26:3 ; Job 32:7 ; Job 32:13 ; Job 33:33 ; Prov 1:2 ; Prov 1:7 ; Prov 2:10 ; Prov 4:11 ; Prov 11:2 ; Prov 13:10 ; Prov 14:1 ; Prov 14:8 ; Prov 18:4 ; Prov 21:30 ; Prov 24:3 ; Prov 28:26 ; Prov 29:3 ; Prov 29:15 ; Prov 31:26 ; Eccl 1:13 ; Eccl 1:16 (twice in verse); Eccl 1:18 ; Eccl 2:3 ; Eccl 2:9 ; Eccl 2:13 ; Eccl 2:21 ; Eccl 7:10 ; Eccl 7:11 ; Eccl 7:12 ; Eccl 7:19 ; Eccl 7:23 ; Eccl 8:1 ; Eccl 9:10 ; Eccl 9:15 ; Eccl 9:16 (twice in verse); Eccl 9:18 ; Eccl 10:1 ; Eccl 10:10 — on solomon's wisdom see above", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2736')\">BDB2736</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2451')\">H2451</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H2454')\">H2454</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2735')\">BDB2735</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2737')\">BDB2737</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>חָכְמה</bdbheb> <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>wisdom</highlightword>, <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 28:3\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(2,28,3)\">Exod 28:3</ref> + 106 t.; construct <bdbheb>חָכְמַת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 35:35\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"35\" vBegin=\"35\" cEnd=\"35\" vEnd=\"35\" onclick=\"bcv(2,35,35)\">Exod 35:35</ref> + 15 t.; suffix <bdbheb>חָכְמָתִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Eccl 2:9\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(21,2,9)\">Eccl 2:9</ref>, etc. + 25 t. suffix; plural abstract emphatic <bdbheb>חָכְמוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 49:4\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"49\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"49\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(19,49,4)\">Ps 49:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 1:20\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(20,1,20)\">Prov 1:20</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 9:1\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(20,9,1)\">Prov 9:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 24:7\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(20,24,7)\">Prov 24:7</ref> <bdbheb>חַכְמוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Prov 14:1\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(20,14,1)\">Prov 14:1</ref> (in correctly pointed as adjective construct f.; read <bdbheb>חָכְמוֺת</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('De')\">De</lookup>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>skill</highlight> in war <ref ref=\"Isa 10:13\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(23,10,13)\">Isa 10:13</ref> in technical work <ref ref=\"Exod 28:3\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(2,28,3)\">Exod 28:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 31:3\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"3\" o